From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sky1: quiet absent optional pin groups on O6N

On O6N (CIX Sky1) the ACPI DSDT describes PinGroupFunction resources for
peripherals that are not wired out on this board (camera: cam_pwren,
cam_5v_pwren; unused USB: pinctrl_usbN; I2S debug:
pinctrl_substrate_i2s2_dbg). The consumer _CRS still reference those named
pin groups, but the sky1 pinctrl provider (CIXHA017) legitimately never
registers a matching group for an unpopulated peripheral.

Root cause is therefore not the driver over-requesting nor a malformed
board: the ACPI tables describe a SoC superset and reference optional pin
groups that are simply absent on this board. The old code fed every such
reference straight into pinctrl_get_group_selector(), which logs
"does not have pin group <NAME>" at dev_err, then forwarded the resulting
negative selector into sky1_acpi_node_to_map(), producing a second
"Pin group cannot be found" dev_err. Result: ~43 lines of benign boot
noise, and (worse) the first absent group aborted the entire ACPI resource
walk for that consumer, so sibling *wired* groups on the same device were
never applied.

Fix the driver side. In process_pin_group_function() probe the controller
group list silently first; when the named group is absent, treat it as a
benign optional group -- log at dev_dbg and skip it, letting the resource
walk continue to the remaining (wired) groups instead of erroring out. This
is the "handle absent groups gracefully (skip, continue)" fix rather than a
blanket log demote: it removes both messages at the source (the noisy
generic core.c path is never entered for an absent group) without touching
generic pinctrl core, and it stops one unwired peripheral from suppressing a
wired sibling. As defense-in-depth for the remaining PIN_FUNCTION path, the
two benign "Pin group cannot be found" dev_err in pinctrl-sky1-base.c are
demoted to dev_dbg -- an absent group there is equally benign on this
hardware.

Kept minimal and self-contained (no dependence on other patches or line
numbers) so it rebases cleanly across 7.2-rcN.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-acpi.c
@@ -534,6 +534,33 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Some boards do not wire out every peripheral the SoC ACPI tables describe
+ * (e.g. camera, unused USB or I2S debug). Their consumer _CRS still list a
+ * PinGroupFunction, but the pin controller never registers a matching group.
+ * Scan the controller groups without logging so an absent optional group can
+ * be treated as benign instead of spamming the console at error level.
+ */
+static bool acpi_pinctrl_group_present(struct pinctrl_dev *pctldev,
+				       const char *group)
+{
+	const struct pinctrl_ops *ops = pctldev->desc->pctlops;
+	unsigned int i, ngroups;
+
+	if (!ops || !ops->get_groups_count || !ops->get_group_name)
+		return false;
+
+	ngroups = ops->get_groups_count(pctldev);
+	for (i = 0; i < ngroups; i++) {
+		const char *name = ops->get_group_name(pctldev, i);
+
+		if (name && !strcmp(name, group))
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
 static int
 process_pin_group_function(struct pinctrl *p,
 			   struct acpi_resource_pin_group_function *ares)
@@ -559,6 +586,13 @@
 	adev = ACPI_COMPANION(pctl_dev->dev);
 	if (ares->vendor_length > 0)
 		state_index = ares->vendor_data[0];
+	if (!acpi_pinctrl_group_present(pctl_dev, group)) {
+		dev_dbg(p->dev,
+			"optional pin group '%s' not present on this board, skipping\n",
+			group);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	gs = pinctrl_get_group_selector(pctl_dev, group);
 	ret = acpi_pin_group_function_to_pinctrl_map(p, pinctrl_acpi,
 						     gs,
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/cix/pinctrl-sky1-base.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/cix/pinctrl-sky1-base.c
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@
 						  info->function.pins,
 						  info->function.npins);
 		if (!grp) {
-			dev_err(pctldev->dev, "Pin group cannot be found\n");
+			dev_dbg(pctldev->dev, "Pin group cannot be found\n");
 			ret = -1;
 			goto out_free;
 		}
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@
 		function_selector = info->function.function_number;
 		grp = pinctrl_generic_get_group_name(pctldev, info->function.group_number);
 		if (!grp) {
-			dev_err(pctldev->dev, "Pin group cannot be found\n");
+			dev_dbg(pctldev->dev, "Pin group cannot be found\n");
 			ret = -1;
 			goto out_free;
 		}
